{
  "$comment": "THE FINISHES OF A READY-MADE SECTION (BATCH LE-15, D2): the wireframe and the seven website personalities of the design deck (docs/web-anatomy/design-foundation/03-components-and-layout-patterns.md, pp. 235-255; RULE P). A section's tree names TONES and ROLES; a finish says what they look like. tones: the colours of a band or card, ONLY theme tokens; an accent is a WORD colour, so it is the theme's link colour (tuned to read as text in each theme — the raw brand read 2.77 : 1 on dark, LE15-49), and muted words on the soft band lean toward the text colour (4.31 : 1 in Light otherwise) (so every finish works in light, dark, midnight and purple; rule 17) — bg, text, muted (secondary words), accent (eyebrow, icon), btnBg / btnText (a primary button on that tone), line (a border). A finish's toneMap swaps a tone it does not use (Minimalist has no colour blocks: strong → plain). roles: type per role, in px (the model's unit; published in rem) — size, weight, transform, spacing (letter-spacing px), italic, lineHeight. The TYPEFACE is the site's (Site fonts), never the finish's, so a page of mixed finishes still has at most two families (RULE D). button: radius px (999 = a pill), secondary 'outline' or 'text'. card: radius, shadow (sm | md | lg | ''), border px. image: radius px. reveal / hover: an entrance (lib/interactions.ts REVEAL_EFFECTS) and a hover (HOVER_EFFECTS) — '' none; reduced motion turns them off on the page (D1 a).",
